Subject: [PATCH 2/4] DirectML: report real VRAM via DXGI instead of hardcoded
 1 GiB

torch-directml exposes no usable memory API (gpu_memory() returns zeros on
the adapters tested), so get_total_memory() and get_free_memory() both
returned a hardcoded 1 GiB. On an 8 GB card that under-reports by ~8x, which
makes every model look too large to keep resident and shows a wrong number in
the UI.

Read the adapter's true DedicatedVideoMemory from DXGI. Reports dedicated
memory only, not the shared-system-memory heap DirectML can also spill into:
overstating the budget is worse than understating it, because DirectML's
allocator aborts the process when a large allocation cannot be satisfied, so
inflating the number turns a graceful fallback into a hard crash. Add
--directml-vram-gb for setups that know better.

Falls back to the previous 1 GiB if DXGI cannot be queried, so behaviour is
unchanged on non-Windows and on any query failure.

Also fix the device banner printing empty: --directml with no argument leaves
device_index at -1, which torch_directml.device_name() rejects.
