From e9e7a8b3c715f631193b2dfbbef845f5538837e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WYSTAF <wystaf@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 07:38:50 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Address review: do not substitute adapters or report
 total as free

Two safety problems with the DirectML memory reporting in the previous commit:

- get_total_vram() fell back to the largest adapter when the bound adapter was
  missing or reported no dedicated memory. On a mixed-GPU system that lets
  ComfyUI size its loads against a card it is not running on, so return None
  instead and let the caller use the conservative fallback.

- _directml_free_memory() reported the whole dedicated VRAM as free. That
  invites ComfyUI to plan loads that cannot fit, and DirectML answers an
  unsatisfiable allocation by aborting the process. Subtract what ComfyUI
  knows is resident, via LoadedModel.model_loaded_memory(), and clamp at zero.

